│   Message:                                                                                       │
│     The patch is submitted (2 files, 3712 bytes): when an endpoint has a response model and uses │
│ the default `JSONResponse`, the response is now serialized straight to JSON bytes with           │
│ Pydantic's `dump_json` instead of going through `jsonable_encoder`.                              │
│                                                                                                  │
│     What changed:                                                                                │
│     - **`fastapi/_compat/v2.py`**: added `ModelField.serialize_json`, which wraps                │
│ `TypeAdapter.dump_json`.                                                                         │
│     - **`fastapi/routing.py`**: `serialize_response` takes a `dump_json` flag, and the request   │
│ handler sets it when there is a response field and the response class is exactly `JSONResponse`. │
│ The bytes are then wrapped in a plain `Response` with the JSON media type.                       │
│                                                                                                  │
│     Verification was limited: 46 tests in the response-model tests passed. One tutorial test     │
│ errored on a missing `email-validator` package, which is an environment issue. I did not run the │
│ wider suite or check the `ORJSONResponse` and custom response class paths. The exact-type check  │
│ means subclasses of `JSONResponse` keep the old behaviour.                                       │
